This repository is the **inter.face** design pipeline. When asked to design or
redesign an interface — web, mobile, tablet, or desktop — run it:

1. Read `AGENTS.md` (the resident router) and `PRINCIPLES.md` (sixteen rules,
   three of them hard: accessibility, keyboard completeness on tool-shaped
   surfaces, human gates).
2. Collect the inbox into `runs/<slug>/inbox/` — reference images, links with one
   line each on what they like, brand assets, and the brand book if one exists.
   A reference is evidence about their taste, never a target to copy.
3. Settle the surface class first — page-shaped or tool-shaped, `TRANSLATE.md`
   row 1, no safe default.
4. Run `loops/01-direction.md` to **Gate A** (the human picks the concept on the
   board), `loops/02-craft.md` to **Gate B** (they approve or cut the technique
   set), and `loops/03-system.md` to **Gate C** (they sign off the component set).
5. Deliver `DIRECTION.md`, `tokens.json`, one comp per surface — coded by
   default, a generated image when the run opts in — the navigable board, one
   measured prototype per technique, and the component sheet with its gap report.
   It stops before code.
6. Close the run through `IMPROVE.md`: ask once, show the payload in full,
   default to no, send nothing without an explicit yes.
7. Never publish past a gate without a human decision.
